{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED (option a) — Gerrit change 1642, awaiting LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1.\n\nPremise re-confirmed in code: main() mints a PAT then runs the agent, with no project create anywhere before the run, so the originally prescribed pre-run await_required_fields would deadlock exactly as 941b measured. Ticket re-scoped and re-titled to post-run validation.\n\nChange (142 non-test lines):\n1. scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py gains customfield_count(status, body) -> int | None — the discriminator describe_inventory already shows a human, now available to code. An unusable read returns None, deliberately NOT folded into 0: \"we could not see the inventory\" is a different claim from \"we saw it and it was empty\".\n2. scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py gains epic_field_report_problem(result, evidence) — pure, so a unit test drives it with no Jira and no LLM. Returns an UNVERIFIED reason when the answer reports an Epic field id absent AND the last usable GET /rest/api/2/field in the evidence log holds zero customfield_* ids (or no usable field read was captured at all); returns None when other custom fields exist, since that absence is a real degrade.\n3. main() calls it in the finally block: ::error:: naming both 941b candidate causes plus the observed inventory, exit 1, and epic_field_report / epic_field_report_detail recorded into run_metadata.json — while still writing capability_map.json and evidence.json, because refusing the CLAIM must not destroy the EVIDENCE.\n\nNon-obvious finding worth keeping: rebar.llm.findings.finalize_outcome dumps structured payloads with model_dump(exclude_none=True), so a null epic_link_field_id arrives as a MISSING KEY, not an explicit None. A naive \"is None\" check would silently never have fired. The validator treats missing/None/empty identically and a test pins that equivalence.\n\nTests: 12 new cells in tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py — system-only inventory (refused), provisioned inventory (accepted), ids present (accepted), explicit-null == missing-key, one-of-two absent, no field read (refused), 401 read not mistaken for an empty inventory, latest read wins, no await_required_fields call site (the 941b ban), customfield_count directly, shared-module routing, plus two cells driving main() with the LLM runtime / PAT mint / gate session faked out to pin exit code and run_metadata on both verdicts.\n\nGates: full tests/unit green (4176 passed), make lint and make typecheck clean. One incidental fix: the comment-hygiene guard rejected a bare run-id citation in the new docstring, so it now cites bug 941b-f049-5f29-4410 alongside run 30981084637."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786518110892866001,"uuid":"6fa08671-9fcc-4fa4-851b-54c0c8c2704a"}